course: dictionary
lesson: 10980
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word warm can mean not cold, keeping you from cold, friendly, or making something warmer. In «Keep your hands warm in those gloves», warm is about the cold. Swap in a meaning and check whether the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Tariq's dad is strict, but he is warm underneath.» Strict and warm sound like opposites, but underneath is the clue. Here warm means kind and caring, not hot. Warm can describe a feeling as well as a temperature: «They gave us a warm welcome» means a friendly welcome.
explain: Warm can also be a verb, a doing word. In «Warm your hands by the fire», warm tells you to make your hands hotter. Ask yourself: is the word describing a thing, or telling you to do something?
fact: Warm can be an adjective (describing a thing, as in «a warm coat») or a verb (an action word, as in «warm your hands»).
fact: «Warm water» means water that is a little hot, pleasantly not cold. «A warm coat» keeps you from being cold.
fact: «A warm welcome» means friendly and kind. It is about feelings, not temperature.
fact: In science, warm means a temperature between cold and hot, and warm air rises.
fact: Mammals and birds are warm-blooded, so they keep their bodies warm. «Penguins keep warm with a thick layer of fat and tightly packed waterproof feathers.»
exercise: «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air; carbon dioxide traps heat like a blanket, so even a small rise warms the planet.» In this sentence, what does warms mean? | Paints the planet | Sends the planet into space | *Makes the planet a little hotter | Cools the planet down
exercise: Mia says, «Her warm smile made everyone feel welcome.» What does warm mean here? | *Friendly and kind | Covered in feathers | A little hot | Keeping you from cold
exercise: «Penguins also keep warm with a thick layer of fat and tightly packed waterproof feathers.» What helps penguins keep warm? | *A thick layer of fat and waterproof feathers | Ice and snow | Staying in the sun all day | Running fast on the ice
test: Tariq's dad is strict and warm underneath. What does warm mean here? | Cold and unfriendly | Red in colour | Hot to touch | *Kind and caring underneath
test: «Warm your hands by the fire.» Which word is the verb (the action word)? | fire | *warm | hands | your
exam: «She wore a warm coat in the snow.» Which meaning of warm fits best? | Covered in feathers | Friendly and kind | *Keeping you from being cold | Making something warmer
